te. Customize individual headings, triggers, and panels on the composed Collapsible sections."},"56":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-32","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"Key"},"57":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-33","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"Action"},"58":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-34","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"`Tab` / `Shift + Tab`"},"59":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-35","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"Move between enabled triggers and controls in expanded panels"},"60":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-36","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"`Enter` / `Space`"},"61":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-37","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#keyboard","content":"Toggle the focused section; focus stays on the trigger"},"62":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-38","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#aria","content":"Each section's trigger is a native button with `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls` linked to its panel."},"63":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-39","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#aria","content":"Each panel is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."},"64":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-40","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Group related sections and keep essential information visible outside the accordion."},"65":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-41","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Use descriptive section titles and heading levels that fit the page hierarchy."},"66":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-42","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Use multiple expansion when users need to compare information across sections."},"67":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-43","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Keep item IDs stable when reordering or filtering data."},"68":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-44","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Manage expansion on Accordion when sections belong to a group."},"69":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-45","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#best-practices","content":"Keep form validation and step progression in application logic."},"70":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-46","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#controlled-state-not-updating","content":"Update `expandedKeys` from `onExpandedChange` and make sure the keys match the item IDs.\nChanging `defaultExpandedKeys` after mounting does not control expansion."},"71":{"id":"/docs/components/accordion-47","page_id":"/docs/components/accordion","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/accordion#sections-close-when-another-opens","content":"Enable `allowsMultipleExpanded` when several sections should remain open together.\nFor a single independent section, use Collapsible without an Accordion."},"72":{"id":"/docs/components/alert","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"page","content":"Alert","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert"},"73":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-0","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert","content":"In-page alerts are non-intrusive notifications within a webpage, providing users with timely information or feedback without disrupting their experience."},"74":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-1","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#installation","content":"Installation"},"75":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-2","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#examples","content":"Examples"},"76":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-3","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#default","content":"Default"},"77":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-4","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#emphasis-variants","content":"Emphasis Variants"},"78":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-5","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#dismissible","content":"Dismissible"},"79":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-6","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#with-action","content":"With Action"},"80":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-7","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"81":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-8","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Keyboard"},"82":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-9","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#screen-readers","content":"Screen readers"},"83":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-10","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#dismiss-button-label","content":"Dismiss button label"},"84":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-11","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"85":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-12","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#props","content":"Props"},"86":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-13","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/alert#alert","content":"Alert"},"87":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-14","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#default","content":"A minimal alert with a title and body text."},"88":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-15","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#emphasis-variants","content":"All 7 emphasis categories. Each variant carries a distinct visual accent and semantic icon so the type of message is never communicated by color alone."},"89":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-16","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#dismissible","content":"When an `onClose` callback is provided, a dismiss button is rendered. The component does not manage its own visibility — the parent is responsible for unmounting or hiding the alert when `onClose` fires."},"90":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-17","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#with-action","content":"Pass a `Button` to the `actions` slot to give the user a clear path to resolve the alert."},"91":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-18","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Key"},"92":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-19","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Description"},"93":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-20","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"`Tab`"},"94":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-21","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Moves focus to the dismiss button or action button"},"95":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-22","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"`Space` / `Enter`"},"96":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-23","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#keyboard","content":"Activates the focused button"},"97":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-24","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#screen-readers","content":"The alert container uses `role=\"alert\"`, which creates an ARIA live region. When an alert is rendered or its content changes, screen readers announce the message automatically — the user does not need to navigate to the alert to hear it."},"98":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-25","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#dismiss-button-label","content":"The dismiss button defaults to `aria-label=\"Close\"`. Override it via `ariaLabels={{ close: '...' }}` to provide more specific context for screen readers (e.g. `\"Dismiss payment warning\"`). This is especially useful when multiple alerts are visible at the same time."},"99":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-26","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Write alert content from the user's perspective: describe what happened and what they can do next, not the underlying technical error."},"100":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-27","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Use `critical` only when the user truly cannot continue without resolving the issue. Overusing it reduces its impact."},"101":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-28","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Always provide a `title` when the alert includes a dismiss button — it improves the reading experience for screen reader users."},"102":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-29","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"When using `actions`, prefer `secondary` or `tertiary` Button variants. Avoid placing a primary action inside an alert."},"103":{"id":"/docs/components/alert-30","page_id":"/docs/components/alert","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/alert#best-practices","content":"Do not stack multiple alerts of the same emphasis; consolidate the message into a single alert."},"104":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"page","content":"Avatar","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar"},"105":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-0","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar","content":"A visual representation of a user or entity, shown as a photo or a monogram of their initials."},"106":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-1","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#features","content":"Features"},"107":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-2","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#installation","content":"Installation"},"108":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-3","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#examples","content":"Examples"},"109":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-4","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#default","content":"Default"},"110":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-5","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#image","content":"Image"},"111":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-6","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#image-fallback","content":"Image Fallback"},"112":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-7","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#shapes-and-sizes","content":"Shapes and sizes"},"113":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-8","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#emphasis","content":"Emphasis"},"114":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-9","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#avatar-button","content":"Avatar Button"},"115":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-10","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#account-menu","content":"Account Menu"},"116":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-11","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#customization","content":"Customization"},"117":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-12","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"118":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-13","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"119":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-14","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"120":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-15","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#props","content":"Props"},"121":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-16","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/avatar#avatar","content":"Avatar"},"122":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-17","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#features","content":"Composable `Avatar`, `Image`, and `Text` parts"},"123":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-18","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#features","content":"Circle and rounded-square shapes at four named sizes"},"124":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-19","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#features","content":"Automatic image loading with a Text monogram fallback"},"125":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-20","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#features","content":"Primary, subtle, and 15 categorical figure emphases"},"126":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-21","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#features","content":"Avatar Button and Account Menu compositions built with Pressable"},"127":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-22","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#default","content":"Use an Avatar with a one- or two-character monogram when no image is available."},"128":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-23","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#image","content":"Place Image before Text so the monogram is available while the image loads or if it fails."},"129":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-24","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#image-fallback","content":"Include a Text fallback so an unavailable photo never leaves an empty identity marker."},"130":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-25","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#shapes-and-sizes","content":"Use circular Avatars for people and square Avatars for organizations, workspaces, and accounts."},"131":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-26","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#emphasis","content":"Use primary or subtle for standard treatments, and a deterministic figure emphasis to categorize entities in a list."},"132":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-27","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#avatar-button","content":"Use `Pressable` to add accessible interaction to an Avatar while preserving its shape."},"133":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-28","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#account-menu","content":"Wrap an Avatar in a Pressable inside MenuTrigger for an account or profile menu."},"134":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-29","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#customization","content":"Use Image native image props for responsive image sources. Choose a deterministic `figure0` through `figure14` emphasis in lists that categorize multiple entities."},"135":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-30","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#customization","content":"When an Avatar triggers an action, compose it with `Pressable` so the Avatar keeps its own shape and receives the interaction behavior directly. Use this pattern for an Avatar Button, or place it inside `MenuTrigger` for an Account Menu:"},"136":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-31","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#accessibility","content":"Give Image meaningful `alt` text when the image conveys an identity."},"137":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-32","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#accessibility","content":"Text remains available to assistive technology when no image loads."},"138":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-33","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#accessibility","content":"Use `alt=\"\"` on the Image and `aria-hidden=\"true\"` on the Avatar when the entire avatar is purely decorative."},"139":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-34","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#accessibility","content":"Give an Avatar Button or Account Menu an accessible name with `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`."},"140":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-35","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#accessibility","content":"When using `Pressable`, provide an interactive role for the non-semantic Avatar child."},"141":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-36","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#best-practices","content":"Use Avatar for informational identity; compose it with `Pressable` for an Avatar Button or Account Menu when it is independently actionable."},"142":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-37","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#best-practices","content":"Use circle for people and square for businesses, workspaces, and accounts."},"143":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-38","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#best-practices","content":"Keep monograms to one or two uppercase characters."},"144":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-39","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#best-practices","content":"Use the same `figure*` emphasis for the same entity wherever it appears."},"145":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-40","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#troubleshooting","content":"If an image is unavailable because of a bad URL or CORS policy, Text remains visible."},"146":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-41","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#troubleshooting","content":"Long Text content is clipped to the avatar shape; provide a one- or two-character monogram."},"147":{"id":"/docs/components/avatar-42","page_id":"/docs/components/avatar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/avatar#troubleshooting","content":"Figure colors repeat after 15 values; assign a deterministic figure emphasis in the consuming application."},"148":{"id":"/docs/components/button","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"page","content":"Button","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button"},"149":{"id":"/docs/components/button-0","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"The Button component allows users to initiate actions or submit forms with a single click"},"150":{"id":"/docs/components/button-1","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#installation","content":"Installation"},"151":{"id":"/docs/components/button-2","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#examples","content":"Examples"},"152":{"id":"/docs/components/button-3","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#default","content":"Default"},"153":{"id":"/docs/components/button-4","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#primary","content":"Primary"},"154":{"id":"/docs/components/button-5","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#secondary","content":"Secondary"},"155":{"id":"/docs/components/button-6","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#tertiary","content":"Tertiary"},"156":{"id":"/docs/components/button-7","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#critical","content":"Critical"},"157":{"id":"/docs/components/button-8","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"158":{"id":"/docs/components/button-9","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#icon","content":"Icon"},"159":{"id":"/docs/components/button-10","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#icons-and-alignment","content":"Icons And Alignment"},"160":{"id":"/docs/components/button-11","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#inline","content":"Inline"},"161":{"id":"/docs/components/button-12","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#minimal","content":"Minimal"},"162":{"id":"/docs/components/button-13","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"163":{"id":"/docs/components/button-14","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#props","content":"Props"},"164":{"id":"/docs/components/button-15","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#button","content":"Button"},"165":{"id":"/docs/components/button-16","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#linkbutton","content":"LinkButton"},"166":{"id":"/docs/components/button-17","page_id":"/docs/components/button","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/button#closebutton","content":"CloseButton"},"167":{"id":"/docs/components/button-18","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"Use the `LinkButton` component instead when you need navigation functionality with a button-like appearance."},"168":{"id":"/docs/components/button-19","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"Use `target=\"_blank\"` to open a link in a new tab without an icon. `isExternal` adds an icon and defaults\nto `target=\"_blank\"` and `rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"`; explicit `target` and `rel` override those defaults.\nYou can also compose an `Icon` as a child independently of navigation behavior."},"169":{"id":"/docs/components/button-20","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"Use the `CloseButton` preset to dismiss an overlay (such as a `Modal`). It defaults to `slot=\"close\"`, so it picks up the overlay's close behavior with no wiring, and always renders an `x` icon with `aria-label=\"Close\"`. For a labelled dismiss action (e.g. \"Cancel\"), use a raw `<Button slot=\"close\">Cancel</Button>`."},"170":{"id":"/docs/components/button-21","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button","content":"Inside a field `Group`, `slot=\"control\"` and `slot=\"trigger\"` pick up the matching look, size, and\ndisabled state from context. See TextField for control affixes, and Select or DatePicker for trigger faces.\nThe `control` and `trigger` variants are field parts: the field sizes them, so use them only inside a field."},"171":{"id":"/docs/components/button-22","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#default","content":"The default/tertiary button is the base for all other buttons in the system. It provides no significant visual treatment other than to provide indication for the user to take a common action."},"172":{"id":"/docs/components/button-23","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#primary","content":"The primary button should be used to indicate the most important action for the user to take in their current experience."},"173":{"id":"/docs/components/button-24","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#secondary","content":"The secondary button indicates an action of secondary importance."},"174":{"id":"/docs/components/button-25","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#tertiary","content":"The tertiary button is the default, low-emphasis style used for common, non-critical actions."},"175":{"id":"/docs/components/button-26","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#critical","content":"The critical button signifies to the user a destructive action will take place."},"176":{"id":"/docs/components/button-27","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#disabled","content":"Any button variant can be disabled to prevent interaction, communicated with reduced opacity and a not-allowed cursor."},"177":{"id":"/docs/components/button-28","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#icon","content":"You may provide an optional `Icon` component to the button. Wrap the text beside an icon in a `Text`. If you do not include text, you must provide an aria-label attribute to identify the purpose of the button. This will produce a square button."},"178":{"id":"/docs/components/button-29","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#icons-and-alignment","content":"Control navigation with `target` and `rel`, and compose icons independently. Stretched inline content follows the browser's default alignment; other variants stay centered."},"179":{"id":"/docs/components/button-30","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#inline","content":"The inline button sits within a run of text, styled like a link while retaining button semantics."},"180":{"id":"/docs/components/button-31","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#minimal","content":"The minimal button is an icon-only button that's used when space is limited and/or when the action is universally understood."},"181":{"id":"/docs/components/button-32","page_id":"/docs/components/button","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/button#sizes","content":"Buttons come in small, medium, and large sizes to fit different layout densities. Without\n`size`, a button follows the surrounding size scope, and uses medium outside any scope. An\nicon-only button is square and as tall as a text button of the same size."},"182":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"page","content":"Calendar","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar"},"183":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-0","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar","content":"Accessible calendar grids for selecting a single date (Calendar) or a date range (RangeCalendar), built on React Aria."},"184":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-1","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"Features"},"185":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-2","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#installation","content":"Installation"},"186":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-3","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#working-with-dates","content":"Working with dates"},"187":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-4","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#examples","content":"Examples"},"188":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-5","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#default","content":"Default"},"189":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-6","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#with-value","content":"With value"},"190":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-7","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#range","content":"Range"},"191":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-8","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#min--max","content":"Min / Max"},"192":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-9","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#unavailable","content":"Unavailable"},"193":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-10","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"194":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-11","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"195":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-12","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"196":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-13","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"197":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-14","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#props","content":"Props"},"198":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-15","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#calendar","content":"Calendar"},"199":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-16","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/calendar#rangecalendar","content":"RangeCalendar"},"200":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-17","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"Single-date (`Calendar`) and range (`RangeCalendar`) grids built on React Aria"},"201":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-18","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"Month dropdown plus a typeable year input in the header for fast navigation"},"202":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-19","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"Keyboard navigable and screen-reader announced"},"203":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-20","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"},"204":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-21","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#features","content":"Date-only values via `@internationalized/date`'s `CalendarDate`"},"205":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-22","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#working-with-dates","content":"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"},"206":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-23","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#working-with-dates","content":"`@godaddy/antares/date` re-exports `@internationalized/date`, the package behind these date primitives."},"207":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-24","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#default","content":"A single-date calendar."},"208":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-25","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#with-value","content":"A calendar with a pre-selected date."},"209":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-26","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#range","content":"Selecting a start and end date."},"210":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-27","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#min--max","content":"Bounding selectable dates."},"211":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-28","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#unavailable","content":"Disabling scattered individual dates with `isDateUnavailable`."},"212":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-29","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#disabled","content":"A fully disabled calendar."},"213":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-30","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#accessibility","content":"Arrow keys move by day; PageUp/PageDown by month; Home/End to row edges"},"214":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-31","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#accessibility","content":"Focus-visible outline; disabled days are not focusable"},"215":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-32","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#accessibility","content":"Out-of-month days render at reduced opacity and are not selectable"},"216":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-33","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#best-practices","content":"Always provide an `aria-label` on standalone calendars."},"217":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-34","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#best-practices","content":"Use `isDateUnavailable` for scattered disabled days; use `minValue` / `maxValue` for contiguous bounds."},"218":{"id":"/docs/components/calendar-35","page_id":"/docs/components/calendar","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/calendar#troubleshooting","content":"Dates not formatting per locale? Ensure the app is wrapped in `<I18nProvider locale=\"…\">`."},"219":{"id":"/docs/components/card","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"page","content":"Card","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card"},"220":{"id":"/docs/components/card-0","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card","content":"A surface that groups related content and actions."},"221":{"id":"/docs/components/card-1","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#installation","content":"Installation"},"222":{"id":"/docs/components/card-2","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#examples","content":"Examples"},"223":{"id":"/docs/components/card-3","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#default","content":"Default"},"224":{"id":"/docs/components/card-4","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#text-lockup","content":"Text lockup"},"225":{"id":"/docs/components/card-5","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#corner-actions","content":"Corner actions"},"226":{"id":"/docs/components/card-6","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#link","content":"Link"},"227":{"id":"/docs/components/card-7","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#grouped-links","content":"Grouped links"},"228":{"id":"/docs/components/card-8","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#media","content":"Media"},"229":{"id":"/docs/components/card-9","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#actions","content":"Actions"},"230":{"id":"/docs/components/card-10","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#multiple-selection","content":"Multiple selection"},"231":{"id":"/docs/components/card-11","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#single-selection","content":"Single selection"},"232":{"id":"/docs/components/card-12","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"233":{"id":"/docs/components/card-13","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#layout","content":"Layout"},"234":{"id":"/docs/components/card-14","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#customization","content":"Customization"},"235":{"id":"/docs/components/card-15","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"236":{"id":"/docs/components/card-16","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#props","content":"Props"},"237":{"id":"/docs/components/card-17","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#card","content":"Card"},"238":{"id":"/docs/components/card-18","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#cardgroup","content":"CardGroup"},"239":{"id":"/docs/components/card-19","page_id":"/docs/components/card","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/card#cardselectionindicator","content":"CardSelectionIndicator"},"240":{"id":"/docs/components/card-20","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card","content":"Card groups related content, like media, text, and actions, on a single surface. On its own, a Card\nis a static surface, or a link when you pass `href`. Put Cards in a `CardGroup` to make them\nselectable or to give them an action: the group owns selection, row actions, focus, and arrow-key\nnavigation."},"241":{"id":"/docs/components/card-21","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#default","content":"A static Card just renders its children."},"242":{"id":"/docs/components/card-22","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#text-lockup","content":"Compose Card with TextLockup for eyebrow, title, and body."},"243":{"id":"/docs/components/card-23","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#corner-actions","content":"Direct CornerActions sit at the top-end of the Card."},"244":{"id":"/docs/components/card-24","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#link","content":"`href` renders the Card itself as a native link, so layered content like an elevated Box stays\nclickable. The link takes its name from its content unless you pass `aria-label`. Do not nest\ncontrols in a link Card."},"245":{"id":"/docs/components/card-25","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#grouped-links","content":"Linked Cards in a CardGroup navigate on a press or Enter. Arrow keys move between rows, and\nnested controls keep their own actions. Disable a Card to prevent its navigation."},"246":{"id":"/docs/components/card-26","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#media","content":"Use default padding for inset media, or zero Card padding with a padded lockup for full bleed.\nMedia can stand alone, follow the text, or be a custom Box. Clip only the media region."},"247":{"id":"/docs/components/card-27","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#actions","content":"Inside a CardGroup, `onAction` runs when the row is pressed or activated with Enter. Nested\nbuttons keep their own presses, so Save does not open the Modal. Compose a Card inside the Modal\nwhen the action is a focused form."},"248":{"id":"/docs/components/card-28","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#multiple-selection","content":"`selectionMode=\"multiple\"` lets each Card toggle on its own. CardSelectionIndicator shows the\nstate, and its children can render custom content from it. Nested buttons keep their own presses."},"249":{"id":"/docs/components/card-29","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#single-selection","content":"`selectionMode=\"single\"` keeps one Card selected at a time. Arrow keys move between Cards, and\nSpace selects the focused one."},"250":{"id":"/docs/components/card-30","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#disabled","content":"`isDisabled` fades the Card. A disabled link Card does not navigate, and a disabled Card in a\nCardGroup cannot be selected, run its action, or take focus. `disabledKeys` on the group does\nthe same by key."},"251":{"id":"/docs/components/card-31","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#layout","content":"Use Grid for responsiveness."},"252":{"id":"/docs/components/card-32","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#customization","content":"`CardSelectionIndicator` only shows a Card's selection state. The `CardGroup` owns selection, so a\nCard stays selectable without an indicator. Pass non-interactive children or a selection-state\nrender function to replace the default circle and icon. See the Multiple selection example."},"253":{"id":"/docs/components/card-33","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#customization","content":"To style a Card by state, target `[data-selected]`, `[data-hovered]`, `[data-pressed]`,\n`[data-focus-visible]`, and `[data-disabled]` from your `className`."},"254":{"id":"/docs/components/card-34","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"A `CardGroup` is a grid: each Card is a row, Tab moves into and out of the group, and arrow keys\nmove between Cards. Name the group with `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Each Card takes its\naccessible name from `textValue`, which also drives typeahead. Plain-text children supply it by\ndefault, so set `textValue` when a Card's content is composed."},"255":{"id":"/docs/components/card-35","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"In a selectable group, Space toggles the focused Card. Without selection, `onAction` runs on Enter\nor a press. Do not combine them: with both, a press runs the action and only Space selects, so\npointer users cannot select."},"256":{"id":"/docs/components/card-36","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"Use Antares controls such as `Button`, `LinkButton`, and `Checkbox` inside a grouped Card. React\nAria keeps their presses independent of row selection and actions. For a custom press target,\nuse `Pressable` and forward its props and ref to the target."},"257":{"id":"/docs/components/card-37","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"Set `keyboardNavigationBehavior=\"tab\"` on `CardGroup` to move through controls within a row with\nTab. Native controls follow React Aria's event propagation rules."},"258":{"id":"/docs/components/card-38","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"A `CardGroup` does not submit form values. Read the selection from `onSelectionChange`."},"259":{"id":"/docs/components/card-39","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"`href` on a standalone Card renders the Card itself as a native link, named by its content unless\nyou pass `aria-label`. A link Card cannot contain controls, so do not put CornerActions, buttons,\nor inputs in it. Inside a `CardGroup`, `href` navigates from the row instead."},"260":{"id":"/docs/components/card-40","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"`isDisabled` fades the Card. On a link Card it stops navigation. In a `CardGroup` it also stops\nselection, the action, and focus, as does listing the Card's `id` in `disabledKeys`."},"261":{"id":"/docs/components/card-41","page_id":"/docs/components/card","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/card#accessibility","content":"On a static Card, `aria-label`, `aria-labelledby`, and `aria-describedby` apply to the surface,\nfor example with `role=\"region\"`."},"262":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"page","content":"Carousel","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel"},"263":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-0","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/carousel","content":"The Carousel component allows users to cycle through a series of content panels (typically images, cards, or text) in a horizontal or vertical layout. It is commonly used for featured content, product showcases, or testimonials."},"264":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-1","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/carousel#installation","content":"Installation"},"265":{"id":"/docs/components/carousel-2","page_id":"/docs/components/carousel","typ