d#features","content":"Provides localized value output, endpoint labels, descriptions, and markers"},"1268":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-30","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#features","content":"Integrates with native forms, keyboard, pointer, and touch interaction through React Aria"},"1269":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-31","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#default","content":"Minimal usage with a single value and min/max bounds."},"1270":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-32","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#controlled","content":"Use `onChange` for immediate updates and `onChangeEnd` for work that should run after interaction finishes."},"1271":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-33","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#disabled","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value is visible but unavailable for interaction."},"1272":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-34","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#labels","content":"Combine an input label, value label, range labels, and helper text when users need additional context."},"1273":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-35","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#value-display","content":"Use `valueLabel` to show formatted values, static context, or output derived from the current slider state."},"1274":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-36","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers","content":"Use `markers` to expose a manageable set of discrete steps for a single value."},"1275":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-37","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#range","content":"Pass a `number[]` to render a range with two thumbs and step markers."},"1276":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-38","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For a single value, prefer a visible `label`; use `aria-label` only when equivalent visible context already exists."},"1277":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-39","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"For an array, provide one descriptive `thumbLabels` entry for every value. Entries are matched by index, so keep them aligned when values are added, removed, or reordered. Describe each thumb's purpose, such as `Lower warning threshold`, rather than its current number."},"1278":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-40","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#accessible-names","content":"`thumbNames` configures native form field names and does not provide accessible labels. Likewise, `valueLabel`, `minLabel`, and `maxLabel` are visual context rather than substitutes for accessible naming."},"1279":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-41","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Each thumb follows the React Aria slider keyboard model:"},"1280":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-42","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Tab and Shift+Tab move among thumbs and surrounding controls."},"1281":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-43","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Right and Arrow Up increase the focused value by `step`."},"1282":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-44","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Arrow Left and Arrow Down decrease the focused value by `step`."},"1283":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-45","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Home and End move the focused thumb to its permitted bounds."},"1284":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-46","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Page Up and Page Down make larger changes."},"1285":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-47","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Directional behavior follows the user's locale where appropriate. Pointer, touch, and keyboard interaction all use the same scale and constraints."},"1286":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-48","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#keyboard-interaction","content":"Markers are decorative and hidden from the accessibility tree. Ensure the field label, thumb labels, bounds, step, and formatted values communicate all required information without relying on marker appearance."},"1287":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-49","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use an array only when every entry has a clear, independently adjustable meaning."},"1288":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-50","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep `value`, `thumbLabels`, and `thumbNames` aligned by index."},"1289":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-51","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use thumb labels that explain purpose instead of repeating the current number."},"1290":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-52","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Keep array values in a stable semantic order. If crossing or reordering thumbs would make their meaning ambiguous, enforce the appropriate ordering in product state."},"1291":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-53","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Avoid large value arrays. Every entry creates another focusable control, which increases keyboard effort and cognitive load."},"1292":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-54","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Set meaningful `minValue`, `maxValue`, and `step` values. The scale should match the precision users actually need."},"1293":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-55","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use markers only when there are few enough steps to scan. Tiny steps across a large range can create an excessive number of DOM elements."},"1294":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-56","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `formatOptions` for currency, percentages, measurements, and other locale-sensitive units so values display and announce their meaning."},"1295":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-57","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `description` for persistent guidance and `isRequired` when a value is required."},"1296":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-58","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `isDisabled` when the value should remain visible but unavailable for interaction."},"1297":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-59","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use `onChange` for lightweight immediate feedback and `onChangeEnd` for expensive requests, filtering, or calculations."},"1298":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-60","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#best-practices","content":"Use a text-entry control when exact numeric input is essential. A track is best for exploring or adjusting values within known bounds."},"1299":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-61","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#a-thumb-is-missing-a-label-or-form-value","content":"Check the same index in `thumbLabels` and `thumbNames`. Each array entry renders a thumb, and its accessible label and form name are read from the corresponding positions. A form name does not replace an accessible label."},"1300":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-62","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#typescript-reports-the-wrong-callback-value-type","content":"Keep the controlled or default value and callback signatures consistent. When inference is unavailable, provide the generic explicitly: `<RangeField<number>>` for a scalar or `<RangeField<number[]>>` for an array."},"1301":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-63","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-controlled-thumbs-do-not-move","content":"The `value` prop is the source of truth. Update the scalar or array in `onChange` without changing its intended shape. For arrays, return a new array so application state observes the update."},"1302":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-64","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#values-snap-unexpectedly","content":"Verify that `step` represents the intended interval from `minValue`. Every thumb snaps to valid positions on the same configured scale."},"1303":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-65","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-final-marker-is-missing","content":"Markers begin at `minValue` and appear at complete step positions. `maxValue` receives a marker only when the range is evenly divisible by `step`."},"1304":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-66","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#markers-are-crowded-or-rendering-is-slow","content":"Increase `step` or omit `markers`. Large ranges with small steps can produce many decorative elements even when users cannot distinguish them visually."},"1305":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-67","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-value-or-endpoint-labels-are-blank","content":"Enable automatic current-value output with `valueLabel={true}` or provide custom content. `minLabel` and `maxLabel` display only explicitly supplied content; neither defaults to a numeric bound or receives `formatOptions`."},"1306":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-68","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#negative-values-do-not-behave-as-expected","content":"Negative values are supported. Set a negative `minValue` and ensure every scalar or array value remains within the configured bounds."},"1307":{"id":"/docs/components/range-field-69","page_id":"/docs/components/range-field","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/range-field#the-range-configuration-is-invalid","content":"Provide finite bounds where `minValue` is less than `maxValue`, a finite `step` greater than zero, and finite values inside the configured range."},"1308":{"id":"/docs/components/select","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"page","content":"Select","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select"},"1309":{"id":"/docs/components/select-0","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select","content":"Select is a dropdown for picking one or more values from a list of options. It renders a labeled trigger and a popover listbox, supports single and multiple selection, and submits naturally inside a form."},"1310":{"id":"/docs/components/select-1","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"Features"},"1311":{"id":"/docs/components/select-2","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#installation","content":"Installation"},"1312":{"id":"/docs/components/select-3","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#examples","content":"Examples"},"1313":{"id":"/docs/components/select-4","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#default","content":"Default"},"1314":{"id":"/docs/components/select-5","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1315":{"id":"/docs/components/select-6","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#multiple","content":"Multiple"},"1316":{"id":"/docs/components/select-7","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#invalid","content":"Invalid"},"1317":{"id":"/docs/components/select-8","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#disabled","content":"Disabled"},"1318":{"id":"/docs/components/select-9","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#form","content":"Form"},"1319":{"id":"/docs/components/select-10","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1320":{"id":"/docs/components/select-11","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#composed","content":"Composed"},"1321":{"id":"/docs/components/select-12","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#props","content":"Props"},"1322":{"id":"/docs/components/select-13","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#select","content":"Select"},"1323":{"id":"/docs/components/select-14","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectoptions","content":"SelectOptions"},"1324":{"id":"/docs/components/select-15","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectvalue","content":"SelectValue"},"1325":{"id":"/docs/components/select-16","page_id":"/docs/components/select","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/select#selectitem","content":"SelectItem"},"1326":{"id":"/docs/components/select-17","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Composable interior**: Compose `Label`, a `Button slot=\"trigger\"`, `SelectOptions`, and optional `Text` / `FieldError`. Nothing is added for you, and what you write keeps the order you wrote it in"},"1327":{"id":"/docs/components/select-18","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Trigger and options**: An empty `Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders the selected value and a chevron from the field. `SelectOptions` is the list in the popover the Select opens: it takes `ListBox` props (including `items` with a render function for a dynamic collection) plus `popoverProps` for the overlay. Write `Popover`, `Content`, and `ListBox` yourself to replace the whole overlay"},"1328":{"id":"/docs/components/select-19","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Composed in another field**: Use `variant=\"control\"` to sit inside another field's `Group`, as a country-code select beside a phone `Input`"},"1329":{"id":"/docs/components/select-20","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Single or multiple selection**: Set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` to allow multiple values"},"1330":{"id":"/docs/components/select-21","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Controlled or uncontrolled**: Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state, or `defaultValue` for uncontrolled"},"1331":{"id":"/docs/components/select-22","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Validation states**: Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` and `isDisabled` for validation and disabled state"},"1332":{"id":"/docs/components/select-23","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Sizes**: The field is a `SizeProvider`. `size` (`sm`, `md`, `lg`) sets the label, trigger, and options, which open at the same size even though they render in a portal. Without it, the Select follows the surrounding scope"},"1333":{"id":"/docs/components/select-24","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**Form integration**: Set `name` and the value submits as part of a native `<form>` (multiple values submit as repeated entries)"},"1334":{"id":"/docs/components/select-25","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#features","content":"**React Aria integration**: Built on React Aria Select for accessibility, keyboard navigation, and typeahead"},"1335":{"id":"/docs/components/select-26","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#default","content":"Minimal usage with a `Label`, items, and a placeholder."},"1336":{"id":"/docs/components/select-27","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#controlled","content":"Use `value` and `onChange` for controlled state."},"1337":{"id":"/docs/components/select-28","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#multiple","content":"Set `selectionMode=\"multiple\"` to allow multiple values. `value` is an array of keys."},"1338":{"id":"/docs/components/select-29","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#invalid","content":"Use `isInvalid` with a `FieldError` for validation feedback."},"1339":{"id":"/docs/components/select-30","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#disabled","content":"Use `isDisabled` to prevent interaction."},"1340":{"id":"/docs/components/select-31","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#form","content":"Set `name` to submit the value with a native `<form>`. Multiple-mode values submit as repeated entries with the same `name`."},"1341":{"id":"/docs/components/select-32","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#sizes","content":"Compare the supported `md` and `sm` visual sizes."},"1342":{"id":"/docs/components/select-33","page_id":"/docs/components/select","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/select#composed","content":"Write the trigger and the overlay yourself instead of composing `SelectOptions`, for full control\nover the popover and the list."},"1343":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"page","content":"SegmentedController","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller"},"1344":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-0","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","content":"A segmented controller is a linear set of two or more segments, each of which functions as a button. A segmented controller allows users to select options, switch views, or sort elements."},"1345":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-1","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#installation","content":"Installation"},"1346":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-2","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#examples","content":"Examples"},"1347":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-3","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#default","content":"Default"},"1348":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-4","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#controlled","content":"Controlled"},"1349":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-5","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#sizes","content":"Sizes"},"1350":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-6","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon--text","content":"Icon + Text"},"1351":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-7","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon-only","content":"Icon Only"},"1352":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-8","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#overflow","content":"Overflow"},"1353":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-9","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#rtl-direction","content":"RTL Direction"},"1354":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-10","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#disabled-states","content":"Disabled States"},"1355":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-11","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#customization","content":"Customization"},"1356":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-12","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"Data Attributes"},"1357":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-13","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#accessibility","content":"Accessibility"},"1358":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-14","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"Keyboard Navigation"},"1359":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-15","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"ARIA Support"},"1360":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-16","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#best-practices","content":"Best Practices"},"1361":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-17","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When to Use a Segmented Controller"},"1362":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-18","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-not-to-use","content":"When Not to Use"},"1363":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-19","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#props","content":"Props"},"1364":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-20","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#segmentedcontroller","content":"SegmentedController"},"1365":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-21","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#segmentedcontrolleritem","content":"SegmentedControllerItem"},"1366":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-22","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#default","content":"An uncontrolled segmented controller with a default selection. The component manages its own state internally via `defaultValue`."},"1367":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-23","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#controlled","content":"Use `value` and `onSelectionChange` to fully control the selected segment from parent state."},"1368":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-24","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#sizes","content":"Three sizes are available: `sm`, `md` (default), and `lg`."},"1369":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-25","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon--text","content":"Segments can include an `Icon` alongside text for added visual context."},"1370":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-26","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#icon-only","content":"For compact layouts, segments can contain only icons. Provide an `aria-label` on each item so screen readers can identify the action."},"1371":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-27","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#overflow","content":"When the number of options exceeds the width of the container, the component automatically shows scroll buttons to let users navigate. Users can also scroll horizontally to navigate the options."},"1372":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-28","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#rtl-direction","content":"The segmented controller follows the current layout direction (LTR or RTL), detected automatically from the browser or system settings."},"1373":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-29","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#disabled-states","content":"Disable the entire group with `isDisabled` on the container, or disable individual segments with `isDisabled` on specific items."},"1374":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-30","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"Components automatically add data attributes for styling different states:"},"1375":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-31","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"**SegmentedController Container:** `data-disabled`"},"1376":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-32","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#data-attributes","content":"**SegmentedControllerItem:** `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`"},"1377":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-33","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Tab**: Moves focus to/from the segmented controller"},"1378":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-34","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Arrow Left/Right**: Move to next/previous segment"},"1379":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-35","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#keyboard-navigation","content":"**Space/Enter**: Select the focused segment"},"1380":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-36","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`role=\"radiogroup\"` on the container"},"1381":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-37","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`role=\"radio\"` on each segment"},"1382":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-38","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-checked` indicates selection state"},"1383":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-39","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"},"1384":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-40","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#aria-support","content":"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"},"1385":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-41","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When switching between 2-5 related views within the same context"},"1386":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-42","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When all options should be visible at once"},"1387":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-43","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-to-use-a-segmented-controller","content":"When the selection immediately changes the displayed content"},"1388":{"id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller-44","page_id":"/docs/components/segmented-controller","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/segmented-controller#when-not-to-use","content":"For more than 5 options (use Tabs or Select instead)"},"1389"