bled` for disabled options"],[1383,"`aria-disabled` for disabled segments"],[344,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1225,"`aria-invalid` for validation errors"],[1773,"`aria-label` (or `aria-labelledby`) is required on the group container"],[1384,"`aria-label` required on the container for screen readers"],[863,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[1171,"`aria-labelledby` associates the visible label when the `label` prop is provided"],[343,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[1224,"`aria-required` when selection is required"],[861,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1169,"`aria-valuemin` and `aria-valuemax` define the range (default `0`–`100`)"],[1168,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value"],[860,"`aria-valuenow` is omitted while indeterminate; otherwise it reflects the current value (clamped to 0–100)"],[1170,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`)"],[862,"`aria-valuetext` and visible value text are omitted while indeterminate; otherwise `aria-valuetext` provides a formatted string (e.g. `\"60%\"`) via `Intl.NumberFormat`; the same string is rendered inside the circle. Override the text with the `aria-valuetext` prop, or control formatting with `formatOptions`"],[2076,"`Box` is a polymorphic layout component that renders as any HTML element or custom component via the `as` prop. It provides consistent spacing, elevation, rounding, and self-alignment within flex or grid containers."],[513,"`Button slot=\"trigger\"` renders a native button with `aria-expanded` for its open state and\n`aria-controls` linked to the panel automatically."],[205,"`Calendar` values are `CalendarDate` objects. Import the date primitives you need from the `@godaddy/antares/date` subpath:"],[252,"`CardSelectionIndicator` only shows a Card's selection state. The `CardGroup` owns selection, so a\nCard stays selectable without an indicator. Pass non-interactive children or a selection-state\nrender function to replace the default circle and icon. See the Multiple selection example."],[1887,"`categoryColors` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[328,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[398,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[416,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[394,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[409,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1824,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[504,"`Collapsible`: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`, and `data-focus-visible-within`."],[514,"`CollapsiblePanel` is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."],[515,"`CollapsiblePanel` uses `role=\"group\"` by default. Keep it when the panel's content does not need\na navigation landmark; there is no need to set it explicitly."]